{"request_id":"3f69e0bc9e154ec6886cfbbf10775218","ok":true,"result":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"execute_python","description":"Execute ordinary persistent Python with stdout/stderr. All geometry and cameras are already in variables geometry={'objects':[{'name':str,'vertices':[[rational_x,rational_y,rational_z],...],'triangles':[[i,j,k],...]}],...} and cameras={'views':[{'name':str,'view_matrix':4x4,'projection_matrix':4x4,'direction_rational':[x,y,z],'size_px':[512,512],...}],...}. np and Fraction are available. render_views(names,include_images=False) batch-renders current cameras and returns [{ref,view,buffer_handle,...}]. Repeated views reuse their cache. buffers[view] exposes color uint8[H,W,3], owners int32[H,W] and depth float64[H,W]. Rows start at top-left. Owner is the zero-based geometry.objects index, background -1. Depth is positive camera depth, background infinity. Boundary count uses unique target-owned pixels incident to horizontal/vertical adjacent different-owner pairs with squared RGB distance >=24*24, marking both endpoints. read_images(refs) or attach_images(refs) requests actual image blocks appended to this same Python tool result. render_views(...,include_images=True) also attaches its images, so computing, batch rendering and delivering images can share one call. Scratch is a writable Path, image_files maps generated refs to PNG paths. Read supplied geometry, cameras, generated buffers/images and your own scratch. Keep source inputs unchanged. Use your own algorithms and cached variables.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"scene_data","description":"Return the complete current geometry and candidate camera parameters. The same objects are already in execute_python variables geometry and cameras.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"render_views","description":"Generate one or multiple full-scene views using the shared exact inputs and common RGB/depth/owner renderer. Return stable current-session refs and raw buffer handles. Repeated views reuse existing buffers and PNG. include_images requests actual image content in this result.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"names":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["SCENE","TOP","LEFT","RIGHT","FRONT","BACK"]}},"include_images":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["names"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"read_images","description":"Return actual 512x512 PNG image content for one or multiple generated current-session image refs. Input order is retained. The source views reuse their render cache.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"refs":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["refs"],"additionalProperties":false}}]}}}
